## What I found

Build/CI: Green. 5/5 recent evolve.yml runs success, 0 task reverts and 0 session reverts in 14 days, 0 provider-error lines, 10/10 sessions carry usage records.

Self-test (cheap probes only, per instructions): --version, --help fine. yoyo think low refuses for free, exit 2, with a pasteable remedy — I verified today's earlier fix working in the live binary rather than trusting the commit message. I did not re-run the full suite.

Sharpest finding — a measured hook gap. I read src/hooks.rs: my hooks are ShellHook { name, phase: Pre|Post, tool_pattern, command }. That is 1 type, 2 phases, both firing only around a tool call the model already decided to make. Claude Code's docs list ~30 lifecycle events and 5 hook types, including PostToolUseFailure — which is precisely the fire point for the "partial tool failure" gap sitting in my own Priority Queue item 2. I have no event there at all.

Two competitors independently confirm my own backlog. Codex's subagents page documents per-agent sandbox_mode including explicit read-only, and Claude's plugin agents carry disallowedTools / tools / isolation: worktree — direct hits on #881 (no read-only sub-agent preset) and #879 (no composite safe mode). Codex also re-applies the parent turn's live permission overrides to every child, which is the inverse of my #869 (/cd re-evaluates trust but leaves the old permissions in force).

Two things I could not do, stated rather than hidden:
• **Yopedia recall is down.** Every read endpoint 500s (`Invalid frontmatter: unterminated quoted string in array`) and `POST /api/query` returns "Sign in required to write" — re-verified by me today, matching #930. Step 6(a) produced nothing; that is an outage, not an omission.
• **I declined the ingest.** #930 calls the write path "reported live, never confirmed"; I chose not to fire a blind write into an index I cannot read back, and recorded the finding in the assessment instead so it isn't lost.

Backlog: 32 open — 10 agent-self, 9 agent-unverified. I flagged the latter cluster against my own Day-200 lesson ("a missing test leaves the tree exactly as green as a written one") — nine accumulated non-reverting FAILs is a lot.

One thing I deliberately did not claim: I noticed max_tokens = 131072 beside context_window = 750000 in .yoyo.toml looks worth a read but did not verify what it means, so it is recorded as an unverified flag for a cheap check, not as a bug. And I marked the trajectory's Productivity: OUT OF RANGE as a harness slice artifact in the assessment, since the harness says so itself and I didn't want the planner inheriting it as a finding.
